 }
 }


}

The problem here is that the charts signal doesn't update the for loop although the console.log(chartsArr); inside it gets logged whenever I toggle the radio buttons.

answer:
The issue likely stems from how Angular handles `OnPush` change detection and signal updates. Ensure your component is set up as an `OnPush` component, which is necessary for signals to work effectively:

```typescript
@Component({
  // Add this line to enable OnPush change detection
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
  template: /* your template */
})
export class StatisticsComponent {
  typeSignal = signal('OIA');
  charts = computed(() => { /* your logic */ });
}
```

Also, ensure that the `charts` signal is marked for check when its dependencies (like `typeSignal`) change. You can manually trigger change detection using `ChangeDetectorRef`:

```typescript
import { ChangeDetectorRef } from '@angular/core';

constructor(private cdr: ChangeDetectorRef) {}

// Inside your radio button group's change handler:
this.typeSignal.set(newType);
this.cdr.markForCheck(); // Manually mark the component for check
```

This ensures Angular re-evaluates `charts` when `typeSignal` changes, updating the template accordingly.

