question:
Laravel 11 - Auto discovery of event listeners inside a custom directory

Before Laravel 11, I used to bind listeners to events inside the App\Providers\EventServiceProvider provider class, for example:
 >
 */
 protected $listen = [
 MyEvent::class => [
 MyListener::class
 ]
 ];
}

In Laravel 11, this binding isn't necessary at all since Laravel auto-discovery feature auto-discovers the listeners from the app/Listeners directory. How can I instruct Laravel to auto-discover listeners from a different directory such as app/Domain/Listeners ?

answer:
In Laravel 11 and later versions, you can instruct Laravel to auto-discover event listeners from a custom directory by modifying your `bootstrap/app.php` file. Specifically, you need to use the `withEvents` method within the `$app->configureEventDiscovery()` call. Here’s how:

```php
$app->configureEventDiscovery(
    discover: [
        __DIR__.'/../app/Domain/Listeners',
    ]
);
```

This configuration tells Laravel to scan the specified directory for event listeners that follow the auto-discovery conventions (methods starting with `handle` or `__invoke`). This setup allows you to organize your listeners in a more structured manner, such as placing them under an `app/Domain/Listeners` directory.

